{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals","id":207154,"title":"what are the rules for embracing supernaturals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-24T08:58:11-07:00","id":207154,"title":"what are the rules for embracing supernaturals?","content":"this is what i know<br /> mages lose their avatars. and magick presumabely the same happens to sorcerers.psychics what ever<br /> garou rarely survive and when they do they become abominations<br /> spirits /demons/imbued are(obviously) unambreacable this is propably true for kuei jin and amenti too.<br /> <br /> so basically what are the rules for embracing changelings/kithain/kinfolk/ these demon hunters from china(i think theyr called shih or sth not sure )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:35:01-07:00","id":207238,"title":"","content":"I know only of Kinfolk, but rules are following.<br /> <br /> Those without Gnosis become normal Vampires. Presumably Gifts that do not require Gnosis go away.<br /> <br /> Those with Gnosis cannot be Embraced, they die simply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T09:51:21-07:00","id":207265,"title":"","content":"IIRC:<br /> <br /> Changelings and their relative splats that have human parts become normal vampires and the Mists sets in regarding their fae experiences.<br /> <br /> Shih, like any other non-Imbued monster hunter goes normal vampire as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:10:38-07:00","id":207286,"title":"","content":"so. ironically kindfolk with gnosis find it easier to resist embrace than garou do?<br /> anyway thanks to both of you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:16:30-07:00","id":207291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=207286#post207286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so. ironically kindfolk with gnosis find it easier to resist embrace than garou do?<br /> anyway thanks to both of you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like an oversight. The Merit mentions a chance to die with dignity, which would imply that they make the same roll, while the rules just leap into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T13:05:56-07:00","id":207432,"title":"","content":"could you tell me what book(and if possible what page) has these rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:42:05-07:00","id":207753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=207432#post207432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could you tell me what book(and if possible what page) has these rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> W20 and W20 Changing Breeds, for the most current. Otherwise, you're looking at a player's guide from one edition or another and Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T02:27:22-07:00","id":208047,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are next to immune<br /> Same with Kinfolk<br /> No clue for Changling, never bothered to touch the line<br /> Wraiths are already dead<br /> Mages become Vampires<br /> Demons are immune, though I think if there's still a human soul in there the Demon gets kicked out and the human is embraced<br /> Kuei-jin are dead and are vampires already, so yeah<br /> Imbued are flat out immune to the curse of Caine, including blood bond<br /> Mummies are immune since they just wake up later if they die<br /> <br /> I think that's everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:40:41-07:00","id":208147,"title":"","content":"Well I'd add that Kitsune burn away as a pillar of fire if tried to Embrace, each and every time no roll's involved, usually taking the would be sire with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:55:33-07:00","id":208314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=208047#post208047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are next to immune<br /> <br /> Wraiths are already dead</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Garou botches a Gnosis roll then you get an Abomination, same goes for some of the Changing Breeds. And there's one thing I would add to Wraiths.<br /> <br /> &quot;There dead Dave. Everybody's dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:14:46-07:00","id":208344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=208147#post208147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'd add that Kitsune burn away as a pillar of fire if tried to Embrace, each and every time no roll's involved, usually taking the would be sire with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other deviance from the &quot;Garou standard&quot;:<br /> <br /> Ananasi can't be ghouled, blood bound or embraced.<br /> Bastet = Abomination that automatically loses Gnosis every month.<br /> Corax = Abomination that lasts until sunrise before burning up.<br /> Mokole = like the Corax, but with a kaijuu rampage lasting until dawn.<br /> Nagah can't become Abominations. In keeping with the Red Dwarf jokes that Wraith spawned, &quot;They just die!&quot;<br /> Ratkin = Abomination that rots away over time.<br /> Rokea = Abomination in a permanent frenzy with a special taste for vampire blood (will go for Kindred over any other potential victims present).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T09:31:30-07:00","id":208408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals#post207154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is what i know<br /> mages lose their avatars. and magick presumabely the same happens to sorcerers.psychics what ever<br /> garou rarely survive and when they do they become abominations<br /> spirits /demons/imbued are(obviously) unambreacable this is propably true for kuei jin and amenti too.<br /> <br /> so basically what are the rules for embracing changelings/kithain/kinfolk/ these demon hunters from china(i think theyr called shih or sth not sure )</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a funny Shih story. It involves a larp game where you know vampires will try anything dumb, so they force embrace the Shih. or try to the Shih uses Qao of the Phoenix to keep getting up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:17:46-07:00","id":208436,"title":"","content":"Embrace a hunter (If you dare), nothing will happend, he will just die...<br /> <br /> Embrace a Demon...holy shit....first of you need to get close to the demon, second of you must avoid at all cost to be killed by the demon in a ridiculous fashion, third of youre fucked..and fourth, i belive nothing will happend.<br /> <br /> Embrace an EARTHBOUND....see the ones i writte about the demon, the fourth one is you break your fangs. (basically, imagine a vampire trying to embrace a rock)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T04:11:41-07:00","id":213367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals#post207154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is what i know<br /> mages lose their avatars. and magick presumabely the same happens to sorcerers.psychics what ever</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer's actually have a better time of it than mages as they get to convert paths over to Disciplines/Thaumaturgy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/757-filli-noctus","name":"filli noctus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:28:46-07:00","id":213437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Embrace a hunter (If you dare), nothing will happend, he will just die... </div> </div> </div>You mean Hunter with capital H? Because normal hunters get Embraced like everyone else, I don't know about chuuni hunters though since I avoid them like a plague.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:20:24-07:00","id":250178,"title":"","content":"The Embrace \u00b7 [Changeling Storyteller's Guide -- Page 85]<br /> <br /> Changelings often don't survive the trauma of being Embraced -- their faerie souls are usually snuffed out by the experience. Any time a changeling is Embraced, the player must make a Glamour roll (difficulty equal to the vampire's Banality + 2). Only one success is needed to survive the transformation. If no successes are gained, then the character's faerie soul is forever destroyed and the character dies. Storytellers may wish to reduce this difficulty for changelings embraced by less banal vampires, particularly Kiasyd and Malkavians.<br /> <br /> Assuming he survives, any Kithain unlucky enough to be Embraced is immediately claimed by the Mists. He reverts entirely to his mortal seeming and loses all access to (as well as memory of) his Arts and Birthrights. The fae soul within the new Kindred is in permanent stasis, and must wait until the Kindred suffers Final Death before reincarnating. Some changeling scholars believe that a faerie soul who suffers such a trauma never returns to this world.<br /> <br /> A Kithain-turned-vampire who is enchanted regains his memories of his fae life for the duration of the enchantment, though as soon as the enchantment wears off, the Mists quickly claim these memories again. An Embraced changeling who is enchanted doesn't regain access to any of his former abilities (Arts, Birthrights, etc.); he simply remembers what he used to be, and what he has lost in exchange for immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3817-sutekh","name":"Sutekh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T17:08:25-07:00","id":250231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sutekh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=250178#post250178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he simply remembers what he used to be, and what he has lost in exchange for immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and then he goes and greets the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:22:17-07:00","id":250356,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there an official posting years ago where it said what happened if you tried to embrace everything, and the Changeling one was:<br /> &quot;Fae: Dead Elf&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T13:34:59-07:00","id":251024,"title":"","content":"I much more prefer supernatural templares don't stack approach of the NWoD, it's far clearer that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T02:30:00-07:00","id":251361,"title":"","content":"Started to write an answer to another topic here... yeah... children can be distracting sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 09-07-2014, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T18:59:28-07:00","id":253754,"title":"","content":"The idea of &quot;things stacking&quot; in CWoD is that it's rare, and when it happens, it's monstrous/nearly unplayable.<br /> A werecreature has to seriously fail on many levels, as it is much easier to simply die than to become &quot;embraced&quot;... they are naturally resistant to Vampire blood in general (they can't even be Ghouls as they can't digest the blood and will throw it up before they can gain any powers from the Vitae.)<br /> An Abomination werewolf is a depressed, lonely, sad creature that is stripped of its connection to the Earth, has lost his connection to his family, has no pack, and is hated by his own people.<br /> An Abomination werecat loses his magic (Gnosis) quickly as time goes on, and werelizards and wereravens have very short existences after their unfortunate embraces.<br /> Mummies, Fae, Mages, Hunters, etc. can't be Embraced.<br /> I suppose a Formori can be embraced, in theory... as a Vampire can be posessed by a Bane, so why not the other way around?<br /> <br /> Truthfully, what it comes down to is &quot;<b>What does the ST want to have in their game?</b>&quot;<br /> Just because a book gives rules on how to make something happen, that doesn't mean that it HAS to happen in their game. An ST should lever let the rules dictate the setting of their game <i>(though, a good ST will always tell their players what is/isn't allowed when/if players ask... or at least elude to the idea that it may NOT be in the setting... if you don't want Samuel Haight in your setting, let a player know if they start to reference him.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T20:51:16-07:00","id":253791,"title":"","content":"Mages can be Embraced. They can TOTALLY be Embraced. It's absolutely terrible for the poor sod who thought it would be a good idea, and they lose a whole bunch of stuff, but nothing short of a very specific and prepared-ahead-of-time spell would stop them from becoming Kindred, just like any other human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:54:36-07:00","id":254497,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the history of the Tremere clan relies pretty heavily on mages being embraceable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T14:32:46-07:00","id":254621,"title":"","content":"Feel sorry for any Abomination that survives. They are eternally at half dice pool for everything. I played one in a campaign at the request of the storyteller. He wanted to involve Garou in the Vampire chronicle and I knew more about W:tA than all the rest of the group combined, including him, so he asked me to make an Abomination for my character. Against my better judgment I made the character and played it. After two sessions of him seeing just how not-like-Underworld they were he suggested, to my relief, that the poor wretched thing watch the sun rise and I made a Gangrel who used to be a kinfolk to fill the role he wanted in the group. He was still a chronically depressed character, but not to the level of an Abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3842-sisk","name":"Sisk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:54:37-08:00","id":345715,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Werewolf</b></u><br /> <br /> Shape Shifters who have 0 Gnosis at the time of embrace can be turned pretty easily. Those with current points in their Gnosis pool however are exceedingly difficult to embrace. Some also have horrible side effects when embraced. For example anyone tied to Helios (such as the Corax) end up dying from the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Abominations however do have a silver lining if you are willing to go truly dark. Sign on up with the Bane spirits and you're good to go. No more Gnosis loss, no more reduced dice pools, etc... Though it's unlikely your ST would let you play that character anymore.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk can be turned like any other human. They have zero protection unless they bought the Merit: Gnosis 1-3 (5-7pts). Then they have the similar rolls that Shape Shifters get to not be turned. When turned they lose their Gnosis if they had it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Changeling</b></u><br /> <br /> Fae can be turned. Their fae side goes into the Mists and they don't remember or get to use anything. If they get Enchanted they get to remember only for the length of the Enchantment. Upside is that if they die their Fae side is released and can be reborn. Unless they're a Sidhe, but that's a different story.<br /> <br /> Kinain (Changeling version of Kinfolk) can be ghouled, turned, etc... They have no protection.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Mage</b></u><br /> <br /> Mages have their Avatars destroyed and ripped apart. They no longer recycle and cannot reincarnate ever again.<br /> <br /> Sorcerors can be turned and have no special protection. A nice ST would allow them to swap some of their Numina into Thaumaturgy, but technically you lose all of it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Vampire</b></u><br /> <br /> Kuei-jin are messed up man. They're less vampires and more escaped demon skin walkers imo (totally personal opinion). But no, you can't embrace them. They're technically vampires by the WoD system.<br /> <br /> Imbued cannot be embraced. Lumped them in since Hunters Hunted is a Vampire book. Regular hunters can be embraced.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Wraith</b></u><br /> <br /> All of the creatures of the Underworld cannot be embraced. They're all spirits, wraiths, oblivion spawn, etc... They're already dead.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Rest</b></u><br /> <br /> Mummies cannot be embraced. They are protected.<br /> <br /> For Demons I don't remember. Someone else may know the rules and the specific book for reference. I can tell you however that their body is technically a human being that they are possessing. Also they make pretty clear statements about how Demons must possess a human, specifically a living human being.<br /> <br /> Demon Hunters can be embraced and the Shih have no special protection. An interesting question however would be how well the cyberware from a Strike Force Zero would interact with a vampire. Especially a western vampire with no Chi or Yang.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Side Details</b></u><br /> <br /> For the specifics on the minutia you need to look it up within each book. Such as the Gnosis rolls to avoid be turned, etc... A freebie is Changelings and Kinain who have vampire blood in their system cannot regain Glamour or learn new Arts or Realms. Also Gypsies who are embraced are the only Vampire that can actually use their original powers. A Vampire who had Gypsy powers can drink the blood of a Gypsy who has the same powers they did. If they do so they can use those blood traits to power/fuel the Gypsy powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T07:51:31-08:00","id":345759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>Changeling</b></u><br /> <br /> Fae can be turned. Their fae side goes into the Mists and they don't remember or get to use anything. If they get Enchanted they get to remember only for the length of the Enchantment. Upside is that if they die their Fae side is released and can be reborn. Unless they're a Sidhe, but that's a different story. </div> </div> </div>Unless your taking a page off from the new, upcoming, V20DA that updates the Kiasyd into being result of Changeling or Kinain Embraces. Considering their own Discipline basically makes htem permanently, more or less, Enchanted the question is do the Mists interfere? It seems to be each ST's own call for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:50:15-08:00","id":346137,"title":"","content":"I was always under the impression that if a Mage was Embraced, their Avatar was simply released back into the Wheel, or it still resides within the once-Mage but being technically dead they were barred access to it.<br /> The only way I know of an Avatar being completely destroyed is through Gilgul.<br /> But I could be wrong :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:32:23-08:00","id":346191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=345715#post345715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Werewolf</b></u><br /> <br /> Shape Shifters who have 0 Gnosis at the time of embrace can be turned pretty easily. Those with current points in their Gnosis pool however are exceedingly difficult to embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporary rating doesn't matter. Permanent Gnosis is the dice pool that gets rolled, and it makes it easy to die instead of becoming a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Gypsies who are embraced are the only Vampire that can actually use their original powers. A Vampire who had Gypsy powers can drink the blood of a Gypsy who has the same powers they did. If they do so they can use those blood traits to power/fuel the Gypsy powers. </div> </div> </div>If you're using that book, you have more problems than just crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T02:53:30-08:00","id":346557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=345759#post345759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your taking a page off from the new, upcoming, V20DA that updates the Kiasyd into being result of Changeling or Kinain Embraces. Considering their own Discipline basically makes htem permanently, more or less, Enchanted the question is do the Mists interfere? It seems to be each ST's own call for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edited: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> A Kithain-turned-vampire who is enchanted regains his memories of his fae life for the duration of the enchantment, though as soon as the enchantment wears off, the Mists quickly claim these memories again. An Embraced changeling who is enchanted doesn't regain access to any of his former abilities (Arts, Birthrights, etc.); he simply remembers what he used to be, and what he was lost in exchange for immortality.</span></span><br /> <br /> Couldn't find the Enchanted rules where I got that, but as far as I remember becoming Enchanted requires a Changeling (or something appropriate from that 'verse) and the use of Glamour. This isn't a perfect/mirrored example but imagine the difference between how a Garou goes into the Umbra compared to a Mage. Similar effects, but it's not remotely the same thing.<br /> <br /> As to the change of origin story on the Kiasyd, the new DA rules once finalized could do two things. Trump the old mechanics and make them Enchanted, or offer such a compelling back story to justify to a ST or group of players that they should be by default. However keep this in mind about Changeling. Banality and Glamour are the life blood of the heart of that game. Humans (or supernaturals) being Enchanted is supposed to be a *huge* deal, sometimes the focus on an entire Story. Verbenna and Fianna are closely tied to the fae in the Tradition/Tribe books, yet even they are not Enchanted. Edit fixed for stupidity. Kinain have Glamour.<br /> <br /> Fae Sight V20 version: The Kiasyd's knowledge of magic isn't just theoretical. Their strangely-colored eyes are capable of detecting the arcane energies of the fae, as well as magic from other, more esoteric sources. They are not, however, capable of using this power to detect the residue of ghosts or vampiric magic.<br /> System: The Kiasyd sees faeries and other fae-touched mortals for what they really are, with no roll required. Additionally, the player can detect any form of magic that does not stem from ghosts or the undead, including magic from mages, werewolves, and other such odd sources. The character can recognize these for what they truly are, provided he has seen similar effects before.<br /> <br /> Nothing there indicates Enchanted to me in any shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","user":"Skeleton Jack","date":". 12-21-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T03:09:22-08:00","id":346563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=346191#post346191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temporary rating doesn't matter. Permanent Gnosis is the dice pool that gets rolled, and it makes it easy to die instead of becoming a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're using that book, you have more problems than just crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Found the W20 rules, I remembered wrong. I swear I read somewhere that at 0 temp Gnosis it changed the roll/effect. Maybe it was an older edition or a house rule an old ST of mine used. Not sure.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">In the event that any Changer is Embraced by a vampire and the Storyteller wishes to leave the result up to chance, the player rolls Gnosis (difficulty 6). Success gives a clean and final death. Failure produces a torturous but equally final death. If the roll botches:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Garou become what are known as Abominations -- a vampire-werewolf. This miserable wretch gains its sire's clan weakness, three dots of Disciplines, and undead nature. It may spend Blood Points like any other vampire (see V20) for the same benefits. On the other hand, it can no longer gain Renown or rise in rank, regenerate wounds without spending Blood Points, or successfully execute any non-Wyrmish rites. Only Banes will teach it new Gifts. At the time of death, all dedicated items and attuned fetishes lose their connection to the corpsewolf. The Abomination cannot spend Blood Points in the same turn it uses Rage or Gnosis for any purpose. Finally, any Abomination with a Gnosis rating below 7 exists in a state of permanent Harano, perpetually able to feel Gaia's grace and glory only by their absence from its soul. The Abomination's Gnosis trait acts as Humanity would for a vampire; any violation of the Litany causes the wretch to roll Gnosis (difficulty 7); a failure means it loses a permanent point of Gnosis. The Abomination can never raise its Gnosis naturally. When the Abomination's Gnosis is all gone, it can no longer step sideways or use any Gifts or fetishes, and is little more than a feral beast.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">There is only one way for an undead werewolf to avoid this fate -- by offering itself utterly to the Wyrm (or, more precisely, to one of its powerful manifestations, such as a Maeljin Incarna). The Abomination's Gnosis is safe thereafter, as the Wyrm sees to fueling its spiritual energy. However, the horror must obey all the commands of its new patron in both letter and spirit afterward; it loses any semblance of the free will to resist or misinterpret the Corrupter's wishes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ajaba</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> Abominations work in the same manner as Garou, save that they lose Gnosis for violating the particular commandments handed to their people by Gaia, rather than the Garou Litany.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ananasi</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> simply cannot be Embraced (or even turned into a ghoul) -- their system violently rejects vampire blood; in death, it sits insert in a werespider's mouth and throat, doing nothing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Bastet</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> may be Embraced, but if anything suffer an even more pathetic fate than Garou. Every 28 days, the Bastet automatically loses one dot of permanent Gnosis until it is a mindless cannibal corpse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">A </span></span><b>Corax</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> Abomination will at least be quickly released from its suffering -- it bursts into flames and dies the Final Death when Helios rises, even if it is hidden from his rays.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Gurahl</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">, sadly, may suffer the Wyrm's ultimate degradation in the same fashion as Garou, save that they lose Gnosis for violating the Code of Ursa.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kitsune</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> are protected from becoming Abominations; Bai Mianxi has bargained with Helios, Luna, and Gaia to ensure it. An Embraced Kitsune instantly dies the Blood-Fire Death: its body erupts into a brief but incredibly intense pillar of flame, leaving behind nothing but a pile of ash (possibly two piles, if its would-be sire can't get away quickly enough).</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mokol\u00e9</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> Abominations die at sunrise like their Corax counterparts. Unlike the wereravens, and unfortunately for everyone in the area (including its sire), a Mokol\u00e9 Abomination spends the entirety of its short unlife in a brutal, mindless frenzy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Nagah</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> subjected to the Embrace simply die; a botched Gnosis roll only prolongs their death throes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Nuwisha</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> cannot be Embraced; they die peacefully without the need to make a Gnosis roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ratkin</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> are susceptible to the Embrace, but suffer perhaps the most gruesome fate of any of the Changing Breeds. Whatever force suspends a vampire's body at the time of death doesn't work for the Ratkin; its corpse undergoes a normal cycle of rot and decay even as it drags itself through the night, until nothing remains but a pile of sun-flammable bones. Whether the ratkin remains conscious after the brain rots away is a matter of shuddersome speculation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Rokea</b><span style=\"color:#53322D\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> are susceptible to the Embrace, though it would be better for everyone -- especially the foolish sire -- if they weren't. A Rokea Abomination instantly loses all of its Gnosis, and spends the rest of its existence in a blood-fueled hunger frenzy. This newly awakened bloodlust seems particularly prone to diablerie; the vampire wereshark prioritizes vampires before any other targets in a crowd.</span></span><br /> <br /> As to the Gypsy book it exists and it was printed by the company. I will not be drawn into any form of debate over it's status beyond saying it's an official WW product. The mechanic specific to vampires and gypsies is very interesting to me as it's a one of a kind exemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T05:21:23-08:00","id":346587,"title":"","content":"I think the DA20 Kiasyd model is a much more simple and elegant solution that allows for playabilty without going crazy. That is to say changelings/high blood Kinain generally die but those who survive become theirown weird bloodline taking 2 in clans from the parent and gaining mythercieria. I'd be prone to run Abominations and Mage Embraces similarly but with different discplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T08:26:39-08:00","id":346674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=346563#post346563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Gypsy book it exists and it was printed by the company. I will not be drawn into any form of debate over it's status beyond saying it's an official WW product. The mechanic specific to vampires and gypsies is very interesting to me as it's a one of a kind exemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>So was Children of Gaia Revised. Of the two, it's not the worst, and most people draw the line well before it. Then we add on the terrible twosome of 2e tribebooks, Fianna and Get of Fenris. They were all published, but none of them was a good idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T13:57:34-08:00","id":347657,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it's not most fortunate depiction of Roma people, to put it mildly. So ignore that book's existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:42:10-08:00","id":348234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals#post207154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>what are the rules for embracing supernaturals?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The basic rule is: Prevent Power Creep!<br /> <br /> Like many, I plunged into the World of Darkness like a Sperm Whale preparing to hunt squid at the bottom of the ocean. There I reveled in its Epic story. That epic story, weaving together all the facets of Creation, Preservation, and Destruction (Wild, Weaver, and Wyrm) from the formation of the loom to the intricate details rendered by the multi-colored threads is the story I enjoy the most. But there is a problem when you play in the games of gods - it is world wrecking, paradigm pummelling, universe vaporizing power. And what can destroy a universe can not only end, but destroy a story.<br /> <br /> In the original game the greatest representation of this Power Creep was a man named, &lt;drum roll please&gt;: Samuel Haight. He was designed to be that really OMG NPC that everyone could really get behind hating. His background combined knowledge from and stolen power of Garou, Vampires, and Mages. He was a kinfolk-ghoul-sorceror who through an artifact acquired an arete rating. His obliteration was a necessity of the game, albeit the PCs were &quot;mystically&quot; able to render him neutralized.<br /> <br /> It is not impossible for crossover characters to be created which carry the flavor of their origin, by maintaining what I will call their genre. For example, the Kiasyd are a fusion of vampire and fae - but they are vampires only. The Gangrel are vampire skin changers so to speak. The Tremere are an example of what mages could become. And if a wraith or geist could be imbued into vampiric form, it would be some deviant bloodline of Cappadocius no doubt with appropriate necromantic powers. However, only one template can be dominant as a means of preventing more Sam Haights. (Oh, the horror of conceiving him in a plurality of being.)<br /> <br /> So, there are ways to handle cross over characters, but the new Template dominates. All powers inspired from the old genre must be performed inherently with the supernatural advantage and style of the new template. This means changing their description entirely to something appropriate to the new genre and balancing it in both story and mechanics. As a werewolf changes shape because of the innate qualities of what they are, a vampire changes shape through harnessing the Curse of Caine in their blood. The newly turned werewolf must embrace that curse, fall further into the corruption they were born to hate, in order to advance their disciplines. What effects will that self-loathing descent into madness bludgeon upon them? In developing rituals to emulate effects similar to previously held gifts - what corrupted form will such a ritual take so as to starkly manifest as a mockery anathema to what is Garou?<br /> <br /> The story of one embraced (against their will?) - becoming something they would not otherwise be, is a wonderful opportunity to explore. But what is the purpose in the exploration? If it is only to be a powerful baddy, then I would scrap it and do something else. If it is to divine the moral culpabilities and brilliant but brief exposures of the good and the better, then tell the story in those merits. Afterall, it is not the powers which make the story, but the character and the crucible; The other is just CGI on the brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 12-23-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T06:10:58-08:00","id":357430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=346137#post346137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always under the impression that if a Mage was Embraced, their Avatar was simply released back into the Wheel, or it still resides within the once-Mage but being technically dead they were barred access to it.<br /> The only way I know of an Avatar being completely destroyed is through Gilgul.<br /> But I could be wrong :P</div> </div> </div> </div>according to mage st hand book death severs the avatar. the embrace isalways preceded by death so it always leave even tremere and his inner circle when casting their ritual dies fora few moments before they rosea s vampires. nowa good question is whether or not the avatar reincarnates or waits for the former mage to meet final death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T07:44:34-08:00","id":357461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=357430#post357430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">according to mage st hand book death severs the avatar. the embrace isalways preceded by death so it always leave even tremere and his inner circle when casting their ritual dies fora few moments before they rosea s vampires. nowa good question is whether or not the avatar reincarnates or waits for the former mage to meet final death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatar is severed as if the Mage had died ergo it reincarnates as per usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T15:38:03-08:00","id":365810,"title":"","content":"So, if that's the way a particular ST runs with the metaphysics, it's entirely possible for a Kindred to encounter their own soul bopping around wearing a new face. Should they ever recognize it, I'm certain that would lead to a <i>very</i> interesting story, rife with personal questions and realizations of &quot;What, truly, have I become?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T17:52:29-08:00","id":366771,"title":"","content":"Been reading the Sorcerer book, the example they give of an African hedge wizard getting embraced has his paths translate into 3 dots of Protean, a dot of Thaumaturgy and 2 dots of Necromancy! (maybe Koldunic sorcery might have been more appropriate since his magic was more about spirits?)<br /> <br /> With the possibility of gaining a childe with that kind of crazy spread you'd think that sorcerers would be a target for embrace by almost everyone, not just the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-11-2015, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T19:16:29-08:00","id":366807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=365810#post365810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if that's the way a particular ST runs with the metaphysics, it's entirely possible for a Kindred to encounter their own soul bopping around wearing a new face. Should they ever recognize it, I'm certain that would lead to a <i>very</i> interesting story, rife with personal questions and realizations of &quot;What, truly, have I become?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>it's very complicated i'mafraid<br /> <br /> avatars are not souls despite the fact that some books seem to contradict it. theyr more like pieces of god really(perhaps not a perfect analogy but best i got) <br /> <br /> souls may or may not be the consciousness. of course one could argue that an A.I still can't awaken. however i would say that it's just that avatars know how to tell the difference<br /> <br /> and then there is the fact that you need spirit to make true life so this could mean many things<br /> <br /> a: using spirit when making life attracts an avatar to the newly created person. but it only works at the moment of creation thus restoring a gilguled'savatar like that is not an option.<br /> b) a soul is indeed different from a consciousness and by giving one to your creation you also givean avatar coincidentally.<br /> c) if so i wonder if one could give a soul to an already existing robot for instance<br /> d) of course when toe corebook talks about &quot;can't reincarnate if you don't add spirit&quot; may not talk about avatar reicnarnation but about consciousness or soul reincarnation<br /> this leads to the question of wheher souls(or consciousnesses if theyare the same) reincarnate and not just avatars. i think that some books on eastern groups imply that they believe that both do but i'm just not certain<br /> <br /> like i said it's complicated<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T19:17:12-08:00","id":366809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/207154-what-are-the-rules-for-embracing-supernaturals?p=366771#post366771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been reading the Sorcerer book, the example they give of an African hedge wizard getting embraced has his paths translate into 3 dots of Protean, a dot of Thaumaturgy and 2 dots of Necromancy! (maybe Koldunic sorcery might have been more appropriate since his magic was more about spirits?)<br /> <br /> With the possibility of gaining a childe with that kind of crazy spread you'd think that sorcerers would be a target for embrace by almost everyone, not just the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't think that the paths would instantly convert to dots. at most they should be xp freebut instant convertion is to much. just ask the tremere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T20:34:23-08:00","id":366915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon 